Subject: soc: sunxi: mbus: add the A10/A20 Mali GPU

On A10 and A20 the Mali-400 GPU is an MBUS master. Like the display
engine, CSI and video engine it sees DRAM at bus address 0 rather than
at PHYS_OFFSET, so it needs the same DMA offset. Without it, lima hands
the GPU CPU physical addresses.

On boards with 1 GiB of DRAM the DRAM controller decodes 30 address
bits, the extra PHYS_OFFSET bit wraps around and the GPU still hits the
right location, so the bug went unnoticed. On 2 GiB boards such as the
Cubietruck every GPU access lands 1 GiB away from the intended data:
the first job fails with GP/PP MMU page faults on page tables that are
intact in memory, or with "invalid command" errors, and the display
stays black once Xorg/glamor or a compositor starts.

The vendor Utgard r3p0 driver for sun7i subtracts PHYS_OFFSET from
every address it hands to the GPU (page tables and buffers alike),
which is why the Mali works on these boards with the legacy 3.4 kernel.

Tested on a Cubietruck (A20, 2 GiB): kmscube and an LXQt desktop on
Xorg/glamor now run without lima errors. A Cubieboard2 (A20, 1 GiB)
keeps working. Not tested on A10 hardware.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
